<title>NETHERLANDS: Bangert cuts DSM estimates, maintains Hold.</title>
<headline>Bangert cuts DSM estimates, maintains Hold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of prelim results flash.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>DSM		 Chemicals     175.00  Bangert Pontier</p>
<p>COMMENT: Hold (unchanged). DSM's 1996 results indication likely to be conservative, but is still disappointing. Peak of current cycle seen early 1998, then general economic slowdown and increased capacity will start to depress DSM's key hydrocarbons and polymers business. DSM can still benefit from economic upturn in main Euro-markets (Germany, France) and has some 12-15 months of growth potential left. This scenario already incorporated in share price, dividends unchanged.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	29.70   (n/a)     4.4	8.00</p>
<p>    1996		   24.50   (26.45)   7.1     10.00</p>
<p>    1997		   29.15   (30.65)   6.0     10.00</p>
<p>    1998		   26.85   (28.55)   6.5     10.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
